  "evidence_2026_09_05_D1S1E": {
    "purpose": "Second, disjoint batch of 38 corrections (distinct file set from the original 6 above). Root cause: home-lock.v1.json's recorded sha256 for these 38 apps/web/public/spark-dash/*.svg entries was computed from a LOCAL WORKING-TREE read that had stray CRLF line-ending conversion (leftover from a past core.autocrlf setting on this Windows machine, invisible to `git status` due to its stat-cache fast path), not from the canonical committed git blob. The values below are each the sha256 of `git cat-file -p HEAD:<path>` at candidate HEAD 90701431b1eb9008c3ccb00ce6d34987e1004193 - i.e. the actual bytes any clean checkout (every CI runner, any fresh clone) receives.",
    "proof": "Exhaustive, not sampled: all 47 current lock+corrections entries were re-hashed 3 ways (lock-declared, working-tree disk, git HEAD blob) and every one of these 38 (and only these 38) showed lock==disk!=blob. A second pass then normalized CRLF->LF on both the disk and blob bytes for all 38 and found byte-for-byte identical results in all 38/38 - i.e. the only difference is line-ending representation, zero visual/semantic content change to the actual approved artwork.",
    "evidence": [
      "_audit-d0-20260904/session-1e-correction/scripts/analyze-home-lock-hash-drift.cjs",
      "_audit-d0-20260904/session-1e-correction/logs/d1s1e-home-lock-hash-drift-full.json",
      "_audit-d0-20260904/session-1e-correction/scripts/verify-crlf-only-diff.cjs",
      "_audit-d0-20260904/session-1e-correction/logs/d1s1e-crlf-only-diff-verification.json"
    ],
    "remoteFailureThisCorrects": "GitHub Actions run 33917667546 (consumer-spark-worldclass / T1 push gate) FAILED at [verify:asset-production-pipeline] with exactly these 38 paths reported as 'Home committed asset replaced' - this was a false positive caused by the lock's own wrong expected-hash values, not an actual unauthorized Home asset change.",
    "didNotChange": "apps/web/scripts/asset-pipeline/home-lock.v1.json (left byte-for-byte untouched, same as the original 6-entry correction's own stated policy) and the actual committed content of all 38 SVG files (git blob content is unchanged - this correction only fixes the ledger to describe it accurately)."
  }
